          "text": "North Carolina Department of Health and Human Services"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Division of Social Services"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "2407 Mail Service Center●Raleigh, North Carolina 27699-2408"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Michael F. Easley, Governor\nCarmen Hooker Odom, Secretary"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sherry S. Bradsher, Director\n(919) 733-3055"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "April 22, 2006"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "**Dear County Director of Social Services**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "**Subject: Federal Outcome Measures Report**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Federal Outcome Measures report detailing data from January 1, 2005 to December 31, 2005 is now available . The report for your county is attached. The statewide Federal Outcome Measures are reported to the federal government as part of the Child and Family Services Review (CFSR) process, in addition to the on-site review of individual cases. The federal government has created six national data standards and benchmarks that states must meet in order to be in substantial conformity on the CFSR. The six data elements are as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "cells": [
            {
              "text": "Six National Data Standards for Child Welfare",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 0,
              "num_columns": 3,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Standard",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 1,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Description",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 1,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Benchmark",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 1,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Recurrence of Maltreatment",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 2,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all children who were victims of substantiated child abuse and/or neglect during the first six months of the period under review, what percent had another substantiated report of maltreatment within six months?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 2,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if 6.1% or fewer of children who were victims of abuse and/or neglect experience another incident of abuse and/or neglect within six months.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 2,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Incidence of Child Abuse and/or Neglect in Foster Care",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 3,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all children in foster care in the state during the period under review, what percentage were the subjects of substantiated maltreatment by a foster parent or a facility staff member?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 3,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if .57% or fewer children in foster care experience maltreatment by a foster parent or facility staff.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 3,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Foster Care Re-entries",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 4,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all the children entering care during the year under review, what percent of those children had a prior foster care episode in the previous twelve months?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 4,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if 8.6% or fewer children entering care during the year under review had a prior foster care episode within the previous twelve months.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 4,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Stability of Foster Care Placements",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 5,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all children who have been in foster care less than 12 months from the time of the latest removal, what percent experienced no more than two placement settings?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 5,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if 86.7% or more of children in foster care less than twelve months experience two or fewer placement settings.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 5,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Length of Time to Achieve Reunification",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 6,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all children who were reunified with their parents or caretakers at the time of discharge from foster care, what percent reunified within twelve months of the time of the latest removal from home?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 6,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if 76.2% or more children reunified with parents or caretakers are reunified within twelve months of their latest removal from home.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 6,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Length of Time to\nAchieve Adoptions",
              "column_start": 0,
              "row_start": 7,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "Of all children exiting foster care to adoption during the year under review, what percent are adopted in less than 24 months from the time of their latest removal from home?",
              "column_start": 1,
              "row_start": 7,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            },
            {
              "text": "A state passes if 32% or more of the children adopted from foster care are adopted within 24 months of their latest removal.",
              "column_start": 2,
              "row_start": 7,
              "num_columns": 1,
              "num_rows": 1
            }
          ]
        },
