    {
      "page_number": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In addition to the six national data standards, the Federal Outcomes Measures report also shows the percentage of children under age 12 in group homes for each county. Although this percentage is not reported to the federal government as part of the CFSR process, it is a number that Congress asks for each year as part of its report from the Children's Bureau. Please note that we found an error in the formula that we used to calculate the percentage of children twelve and under in group care for the last reporting period, so you will see some changes in this percentage. Further, we would like to clarify that children in maternity homes are not counted as part of this statistic."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You will receive a copy of the Federal Outcomes Report for your county quarterly. Each report consists of five columns. The first column names the data standard, the second column lists the federal benchmark, the third column shows North Carolina's performance on the measure, the fourth column shows your level counties' performance, and the fifth column details your individual counties' performance. Eventually, we hope to post this data on a county-by-county basis on the Division's website. We will notify you as soon as this is available. In the mean time, counties can access each other's data through XPTR report \"PQA 182 Outcomes Measures\"."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The Division hopes that the Federal Outcomes Report will be helpful to you. This information can be used to update your staff and the community concerning your progress on ensuring the safety, permanence and well-being of the children in your county and in the state. If you have questions about the information contained in these reports, the interpretation of that information, or the specific programming logic used to develop this report, please contact Kate Johnson at "
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "text": "Katherine.Johnson@ncmail.net",
          "url": "mailto:Katherine.Johnson@ncmail.net"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": " or 919-733-3801."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Sincerely,"
        },
        {
